  "title": "Reflexive Verbs",
  "prerequisiteIds": ["de-lesson-perfekt-sein"],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "explanation", "markdown": "Reflexive verbs like **sich waschen** (to wash oneself) and **sich anziehen** (to get dressed) need a reflexive pronoun that matches the subject: **ich wasche mich**, **du wäschst dich**, **er/sie/es wäscht sich**, **wir waschen uns**, **ihr wascht euch**, **sie/Sie waschen sich**." },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "de-ex-reflexive-1" },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "de-ex-reflexive-2" },
    { "type": "explanation", "markdown": "In the Perfekt, reflexive verbs always take **haben**, and the reflexive pronoun goes right after it: **Ich habe mich gewaschen** (I washed myself)." },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "de-ex-reflexive-3" }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "de-ex-reflexive-1",
      "type": "fill-blank",
      "prompt": "Ich wasche ___. (I wash myself.)",
      "answer": "mich",
      "relatedItemId": "de-vocab-routine-002"
    },
    {
      "id": "de-ex-reflexive-2",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "prompt": "Wir ziehen ___ an. (We get dressed.)",
      "answer": "uns",
      "distractors": ["mich", "euch", "sich"],
      "relatedItemId": "de-vocab-routine-003"
    },
    {
      "id": "de-ex-reflexive-3",
      "type": "translate",
      "prompt": "Translate: \"She washed herself.\" (Perfekt tense)",
      "answer": ["Sie hat sich gewaschen."],
      "relatedItemId": "de-vocab-routine-002"
    }
  ]
}
